\description{
Selects the cold and hot anchor pixels used by METRIC to calibrate the
near-surface temperature difference dT as a function of the surface
temperature, following explicit criteria built with
\code{\link[=ef_anchor_criteria]{ef_anchor_criteria()}}. The selection uses surface variables only (no net
radiation, soil heat flux or weather; stage [A] of
dev/specs/anchor-pixels.md section 1.3), is deterministic and returns a
complete audit trail: the anchor pixels and their attributes, one
calibration point per class, the computed thresholds, the funnel of
candidates, the flags and the provenance. The boundary conditions of
the anchors are added afterwards by \code{\link[=ef_anchor_conditions]{ef_anchor_conditions()}}.
}
\details{
Order of operations (dev/specs/anchor-pixels.md section 5.3): (1)
validation; (2) usable cells (\code{qa} and the search domain); (3) valid cells
(no missing value in a variable used by the criteria); (4) percentile
domain and computed thresholds; (5) rules of each class (all must hold);
(6) homogeneity; (7) final pick; (8) one calibration point per class and
consistency check; (9) flags and audit trail. Each step adds a row to the
funnel.

Search domains and relaxation: for each class, the search domains are
tried in order and, within each domain, \code{criteria} and then the steps of
\code{relax}; the first combination that leaves at least one anchor pixel is
used and recorded. Using a later domain raises
\code{EF_ANCHOR_SEARCH_EXPANDED}; using a relaxation step raises
\code{EF_ANCHOR_CRITERIA_RELAXED}, and \code{EF_ANCHOR_HOMOGENEITY_DROPPED} when that
step has no homogeneity test while \code{criteria} had one. Nothing is relaxed
without an explicit plan.

Other flags: \code{EF_ANCHOR_SINGLE_PIXEL} (a class has one pixel),
\code{EF_ANCHOR_TIES} (a tie at the limit of a \code{"lowest"}/\code{"highest"} pick was
resolved by cell number), \code{EF_ANCHOR_WINDOW_INCOMPLETE} (record scope:
rows of \code{pixels} whose homogeneity window has missing cells or crosses
the grid border) and \code{EF_ANCHOR_OVERPASS_SPREAD}.

Errors: no candidate for a class after every domain and step: class
\code{earthflux_anchor_no_candidates} with fields \code{type} (\code{"cold"}, \code{"hot"} or
\code{"both"}), \code{funnel} and \code{thresholds}; empty percentile domain:
\code{earthflux_anchor_insufficient_domain}; hot calibration point not hotter
than the cold one: \code{earthflux_anchor_inverted} (fields \code{lst_cold},
\code{lst_hot}). All three also inherit \code{earthflux_anchor_error}. Invalid
layers or arguments: \code{earthflux_input_error}; out-of-domain values:
\code{earthflux_domain_error}. A small thermal contrast or few candidates are
not errors and are not flagged: their thresholds have no reference
(class II codes \code{EF_ANCHOR_CONTRAST_LOW}, \code{EF_ANCHOR_FEW_CANDIDATES}).

The selection uses no random numbers and does not modify the random
number generator. Selection on the surface temperature referred to an
elevation datum (decision D-AP-07) is not available: \code{lst} is used as
given.

Verification status: the procedure is a transparent container for
user-stated criteria; no criterion is \code{VERIFICADA}
(dev/specs/anchor-pixels.md sections 3 and 10).
